  "id": "DrugBank_DB06691 - MONDO_1040",
  "verbalization": "Mepyramine is implicated in the pathogenesis of Nasopharyngitis through a chain of indications that link it to common cold symptoms. The evidence suggests that Mepyramine is associated with the Common Cold, which in turn is linked to Nasopharyngitis via different pathways. While the exact mechanism by which Mepyramine influences the Common Cold is not fully elucidated, the shared indication of Nasopharyngitis across multiple pathways implies a potential role in the inflammatory or mucosal responses associated with colds. The presence of multiple indirect pathways, each connecting Mepyramine to Nasopharyngitis through distinct mediators, suggests that the relationship may be mediated by a broader network of physiological processes, including immune activation or mucosal irritation. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship and underscores the need for further investigation into the specific mechanisms by which Mepyramine contributes to Nasopharyngitis.",
